      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I wasn't sure whether to report this or not because I wasn't sure if this was an intended change.\n\nI spent some time trying to get used to this behaviour, and I have to admit that there are some niche cases where it is nice to switch to one-handed mode when tracking is lost, but generally-speaking this just tends to cause one-handed mode to trigger accidentally way more often than it should.\n\nI wonder if one-handed mode should only toggle due to tracking loss if no input/touch has been received from the 'untracked' controller for X amount of time as a compromise? Rather than completely reverting to the legacy behaviour of it only enabling once the controller turns off completely.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
